<article class="env-lemma" id="0CYR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CYR">Lemma <span data-tag="0CYR">30.26.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $Z_ i \subset X$, $i = 1, \ldots , n$ be closed subsets. If $Z_ i$, $i = 1, \ldots , n$ are proper over $S$, then the same is true for $Z_1 \cup \ldots \cup Z_ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Endow $Z_ i$ with their reduced induced closed subscheme structures. The morphism 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Z_1 \amalg \ldots \amalg Z_ n \longrightarrow X  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is finite by Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/035C" data-tag="035C">29.45.12</a> and <a href="/tag/0CYI" data-tag="0CYI">29.45.13</a>. As finite morphisms are universally closed (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01WN" data-tag="01WN">29.45.11</a>) and since $Z_1 \amalg \ldots \amalg Z_ n$ is proper over $S$ we conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/0CYQ" data-tag="0CYQ">30.26.5</a> part (2) that the image $Z_1 \cup \ldots \cup Z_ n$ is proper over $S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>